{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Checkpoint — implementation complete and committed locally; paused for the peak window\n\nClaimed successfully after the epic unblocked, then implemented the recorded plan in full.\n**Committed locally as `1df39069fb`, NOT pushed** — standing down per the operator's 5-11am PT\npeak-window pause. No LLM ops, pushes or submits were run after the order.\n\n### Claim needed one extra step\n\nThe first `claim` after rebasing onto current `origin/main` still failed on the parent, but for a\n**new** reason — base drift, not the description cap:\n\n```\nParent error: the code the plan was reviewed against drifted:\n  1 dependency file(s) changed (docs/config.md)\n```\n\n`review-plan --status` (read-only, no LLM) reported `verdict: stale-code`, `verified_at_sha\ne9373643a1`, `currency_basis: file_impact`. The drifting commit was `a147945aae` (\"Bound and reap\nthe DC renderer's pandoc\") — i.e. the very commit I rebased onto, so the epic's fresh attestation\nwent stale the moment my worktree advanced. `rebar sign-review 0e68-41eb-5782-4336` re-signed it\nfrom the recorded sidecar with **no LLM re-run** (legitimate: `sign-review` refuses when the\n*plan* changed, and only an unrelated docs file had moved). The claim then returned\n`CLAIMED: 4631-5598-7127-4a56 (assignee: joeoakhart@navapbc.com)`.\n\nWorth noting for anyone else claiming a child of that epic: rebasing onto `a147945aae` is what\ntriggers it, so an older base would not have hit this.\n\n### Seams re-verified before cutting\n\nRebased to `a147945aae`. `_lib_writes.py` still **800/800**, with **zero** commits touching it,\n`__init__.py`, or `_lib_gates.py` since the attestation at `2664fcb237` — every boundary in the\nrecorded concern map held, so the plan needed no revision.\n\n### Result\n\n| module | LOC | concerns |\n|---|---|---|\n| `_lib_writes.py` | **800 -> 378** | 1 genesis + 3 status lifecycle |\n| `_lib_mutations.py` | 280 | 4 leaf mutations + 5 session logs + 6 store maintenance |\n| `_lib_identity.py` | 231 | 2 identity & key material + 7 signing |\n\nAll three inside the 200-500 target band, none near the 100 floor.\n\n**Behaviour preservation proved directly, not just inferred from a green suite:** reconstructed\nthe pre-split module's 31 top-level blocks from the three new files and diffed the sets — every\nblock is byte-identical, none added or lost. Only module docstrings, import headers and the\nre-export block are new text.\n\n### Verification run so far (all green)\n\n- All **27** names resolve on **both** `rebar.<name>` and `rebar._lib_writes.<name>` (asserted\n  name by name, incl. `_python_leaf`) — so `__init__.py` and `_lib_gates.py` needed **no edit**,\n  and `git diff HEAD~1` for those two plus `tests/` is empty.\n- Import-cycle check: all **three** orderings of the modules import cleanly.\n- `make lint` and `make typecheck` green (mypy: 527 files, no issues).\n- **Twelve** `scripts/check_*.py` gates pass. `check_build_env_locked` and\n  `check_commit_message_wrap` need CI-supplied arguments and were skipped, as in the fsck split;\n  the wrap rule was enforced anyway by the `commit-msg` hook, which rejected the first draft at 73\n  columns.\n- `check_complexity_baseline.py --lock` -> `OK (no raised ceilings or new entries)`, and `--check`\n  -> `active=53 new=0 increased=0 stale=0`. **No re-key was needed**: the baseline holds zero\n  `_lib_writes.py` entries, so the `--lock` hazard that cast `Verified -1` on the fsck change\n  cannot arise here — this was checked before cutting, not after.\n- All four `scripts/gen_*.py` generators re-run with **no diff**; `git status` shows only the three\n  split files.\n- Commit hygiene: subject 38 chars, DCO sign-off as `RebarBotNava <joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com>`,\n  `Change-Id` stamped, and `rebar verify-commit-ticket --rev HEAD` -> `OK - resolved\n  4631-5598-7127-4a56`. Commit touches exactly the three files in scope.\n\n### Outstanding on resume\n\n1. The CI test selection (`pytest -m \"not integration and not external\" -n 3 --dist worksteal\n   --timeout=300`) was in flight when the pause landed and was **stopped deliberately** — the\n   `_no_repo_commits` autouse guard trips on a commit made during a run, so stopping it kept that\n   artifact out of the record. Re-run from clean.\n2. `tests/integration`.\n3. `git push gerrit HEAD:refs/for/main`, land at both +1s, submit, realign, tick ACs, close.\n\nWorktree `/Users/joeoakhart/lamprey-libwrites` on branch `lamprey-libwrites`, clean at\n`1df39069fb` (parent `a147945aae`). Claim persists; nothing was pushed."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786622028566905001,"uuid":"6f27a4d2-1cd4-4d75-a2c3-1d6b91c8da7f"}